  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A small square loop of wire of side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi></math>&nbsp;is placed inside a large square loop of wire <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>&#8811;</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. Both loops are coplanar and their centres coincide at point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math> as shown in figure. The mutual inductance of the system is</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0053_dab9f251557d.png\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 170px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>",
